  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SimpleXRHoverInfo
  objectName: Blue Reef Wrasse
  description: The Blue Reef Wrasse is a vibrant tropical fish commonly found in
    the warm coral reef waters surrounding Cairns and the Great Barrier Reef. Recognized
    for its striking blue body and colorful tail patterns, this agile swimmer is
    known for weaving through coral formations and rocky reef habitats in search
    of small crustaceans and marine organisms. Wrasse species play an important role
    in maintaining reef health by helping control parasites and algae growth within
    the ecosystem. In this underwater VR experience, the Blue Reef Wrasse adds energy,
    movement, and color to the reef environment, creating a more immersive and realistic
    marine atmosphere.
